\title{Discover and retrieve public ArcGIS data}
\description{
The package includes a catalog of 52 checked layers from Tampa Bay
publishers. Use \code{\link[=tbod_list_datasets]{tbod_list_datasets()}} or \code{\link[=tbod_search_datasets]{tbod_search_datasets()}} with
\code{source = "checked"} to browse the catalog offline. The default also searches
public ArcGIS portals configured for Tampa, St. Petersburg, Clearwater,
Hillsborough County, Pinellas County, and the Tampa Bay Regional Planning
Council.
\code{\link[=tbod_list_portals]{tbod_list_portals()}} lists those publishers.
}
\details{
\code{\link[=tbod_discover]{tbod_discover()}} searches another ArcGIS portal or lists layers in a
FeatureServer or MapServer service. \code{\link[=tbod_get_dataset]{tbod_get_dataset()}} accepts a bundled
ID, discovered row, stable ArcGIS ID, or direct layer URL and returns a tibble
or optional \code{sf} object. \code{\link[=tbod_provenance]{tbod_provenance()}} reads its source and query
record. \code{\link[=tbod_download_dataset]{tbod_download_dataset()}} saves resumable chunks.

Checked layers have saved schema snapshots. \code{\link[=tbod_schema]{tbod_schema()}} reads a saved or
current schema, and \code{\link[=tbod_check_schema]{tbod_check_schema()}} reports changes. Retrieval warns
for compatible drift and stops before querying for incompatible drift.

This independent package was inspired by rOpenSci's nycOpenData; it is not
affiliated with rOpenSci or any government publisher. Government datasets
retain their upstream terms.
}
\section{Request identity}{

Web requests use \verb{tampaBayOpenData/0.1.0} as the default user agent. Set
\code{options(tampaBayOpenData.user_agent = "my-project/1.0 (contact: me@example.org)")}
before calling a function that contacts a publisher to identify your own
application. Set the option to \code{NULL} to restore the default. The setting
applies to discovery, retrieval, and downloads.
}

\section{Live examples}{

Examples that contact public ArcGIS services run when
\code{TAMPA_OPEN_DATA_LIVE=true} is set in the R environment. Without this opt-in,
the examples use only the bundled registry and run offline.
}

